
  <sn><md>### Iceberg

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/Geography/Geographical%20Features/assets/geographica-features-all.jpeg)

* **Definition &amp; Origin:** An iceberg is a large chunk of freshwater ice that `breaks off from a glacier` and reaches the open sea or ocean. 
* **Composition:** Because glaciers are made of accumulated snow, icebergs consist entirely of `freshwater ice floating in saltwater`.
* **Submerged Mass:** Due to the heavy weight and density of the ice chunk, only the `tip of the iceberg is visible` above the water's surface, while nearly **90% of its total mass remains submerged underwater**.
